title: One form, one meaning.
template: landing
---
  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="ex">
    <h2 id="ex">Small programs, real output</h2>
    <p class="note">Each program is a complete file; its output is checked every build.</p>

    <h3>Hello</h3>
    <p class="note">A program can start with statements: no <code>main</code>, imports or semicolons.</p>
    <example name="hello"/>

    <h3>Functions and loops</h3>
    <p class="note">Types first; <code>return … if …</code> exits early; <code>1..=15</code> includes its end.</p>
    <example name="fizzbuzz"/>

    <h3>Structs and enums</h3>
    <p class="note">Methods mutate with <code>ref this</code>; other arguments take a particle, <code>by:</code>.</p>
    <example name="shapes"/>

    <h3>Errors are values</h3>
    <p class="note">A failing function says <code>fails</code> in its signature. Callers choose: <code>catch</code> supplies a fallback; <code>defer failing</code> runs only on failure.</p>
    <example name="errors"/>
  </section>

  <section class="band install" aria-labelledby="go">
    <h2 id="go">What you get</h2>
    <ul class="dots">
      <li>The compiler writes C; <code>zig cc</code> makes the native executable.</li>
      <li>Failure is a value: <code>fails E</code> in a signature, <code>try</code> and <code>catch</code> at the call.</li>
      <li>Memory safety is not a build mode: bounds and region checks apply in every build.</li>
      <li>One spelling per construct: <code>bayan format</code> rewrites any second spelling.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><a href="tutorial.html">Start the tutorial</a>, see <a href="whats-new.html">what is new in 0.4.1</a>, read <a href="parameters.html">parameters and arguments</a> or the <a href="manifesto.html">manifesto</a> for the ideas; source and issues: <a href="https://github.com/ikhbat-org/bayan">github.com/ikhbat-org/bayan</a>.</p>
  </section>
